  "summary": "Little known fact: building websites was how I paid my rent fresh out of high school. At the time, I didn't see a career in Web / Software Development and instead pursued a career in sales. That all changed when the world came to a halt in 2020. I heard that there were actual careers in tech, I took a bootcamp at Flatiron Academy, and the rest is history. Shortly after, I started my first role where I learned a great deal about Software Engineering.\n\nI have developed a wide variety of skills from my previous role at Cognizant and from courses I've taken at Flatiron Academy, Free Code Camp, and Educative. I've taken courses on Software Development, Java Development, as well as SEO and I've received certifications. \n\nI am currently a Lead Software Engineer at Diamond Screens. As a Lead Software Engineer, I acquire my own clients, plan out project requirements, build applications / websites and provide my own customer service. During this role, I have learned the importance of setting expectations with stakeholders. Often times, clients expect projects to be done much sooner than what is realistically possible. I educate them on the process and find compromises and milestones that suit their immediate needs. \n\nI am open to roles as Software Engineer, Software Developer and Web Developer. If you have any questions or would like a copy of my resume, I'd love to connect! Send me over an email to get in touch.\n\nSkills Include: Java, C#, C++, Javascript, Node.JS, Vue.JS, React.JS, Springboot, PostgreSQL, .NET, Agile, CI/CD.",
